  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council. The Unionists agreed not to contest the South Ward if the Nationalists withdrew their two candidates from the East Ward, so only the North Ward went to a poll (Monday 16 January 1905; the Irish News, 18 January 1905, p. 5, reports the North Ward, which it calls St. Patrick's Ward, as polled \"yesterday\"). Declared elected without a poll."
